            "description": "Watch Philippines vs Myanmar highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 9, 2026. The international friendly between the Philippines and Myanmar offered a fascinating look at two sides looking to sharpen their tactical setups. Played on June 9, 2026 , the match provided plenty of talking points for fans of Southeast Asian football . Explosive Action After the Interval As the second half got underway, the Philippines looked to build on their early momentum and put the match beyond their opponents' reach. In the 54th minute, the pressure told when P. B. Tabinsa found the back of the net to make it 2-0, capitalizing on a well-timed assist from C. Mrowka . This goal forced Myanmar to take more risks, opening up space for a thrilling conclusion to this sports spectacle after a hard-fought first half . A Late Surge of Goals The final ten minutes of the match turned into a whirlwind of offensive action, starting in the 80th minute. S. Beraque extended the lead to 3-0 after being set up by S. P. Woods , seemingly putting the result beyond doubt. However, Myanmar showed resilience almost immediately, as W. N. Tun pulled one back just two minutes later to make it 3-1. This brief glimmer of hope for the away side was short-lived, as the hosts maintained their clinical edge in front of goal . Dominant Finish in Stoppage Time In the closing stages, the Philippines continued to push forward, seeking to maximize every chance created. A. Leipold restored the three-goal cushion in the 88th minute, making it 4-1 and effectively ending any thoughts of a Myanmar comeback. The scoring was rounded off deep into stoppage time when S. Beraque netted his second of the night in the 91st minute, sealing a comprehensive 5-1 performance in this international friendly ."
